      "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[-2,3],$ so the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(-2)$ and $f(3)$ inclusively.\n\nSince $f(-2)=6$ and $f(3)=2$, we must have \n$k\\in [2,6].$\n\nTherefore, the missing part is \"$2$ and $6$\".\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14062906/assets/567a6a601c80d1af5adcb10188d6ae4de83aa154505d59945cadbc226f05eb4b.png)",
